    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n1322" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">aequŏrĕus</span></b> , a,
		um, adj.
		aequor, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>of</i> or <i>pertaining to the sea</i> (only
				<b>poet.</b>): 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">rex,</span>”
				<i>Neptune</i>,
				 <i><span class="en">Ov. M.
					8, 604</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Britanni,</span>”
				<i>the Britons surrounded by the sea</i>,
				 <i><span class="en">id.
					ib. 15, 753</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">genus,</span>”
				<i>the ocean kind</i>, <i>fish</i>,
				 <i><span class="en">Verg.
					G. 3, 243</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">aquae,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Mart. 10, 51 al.</span></i>
			</div>
